{
  "slug": "yandex-direct",
  "name": "Yandex Direct",
  "aliases": [
    "Яндекс Директ",
    "Яндекс.Директ",
    "Yandex.Direct",
    "Yandex Direct API"
  ],
  "description": "Let your AI analyse your Yandex Direct advertising, read-only: campaigns, ad groups, ads, keywords and bids, sitelinks and callouts, agency clients, dictionaries, change tracking and statistics reports by day, campaign, ad or search query.",
  "instructions": "## Yandex Direct\nThis connector reads **Yandex Direct API v5** (`https://api.direct.yandex.com/json/v501`) with an OAuth token: the advertiser account, campaigns, ad groups, ads, keywords and bids, sitelinks, callouts, negative keyword sets, retargeting lists, agency clients, dictionaries, change tracking and statistics reports. Every tool is read-only; nothing here creates, changes, pauses or pays for anything.\n\n**Setup (about 10 minutes, once)**\n1. Register an app at https://oauth.yandex.ru (platform: web services, permission **Yandex Direct API**, `direct:api`). Note its ClientID.\n2. In the Yandex Direct web interface open **Tools, API** and submit an API access request for that ClientID (it needs at least one campaign in the account; approval takes from an hour to a few business days). Accept the API user agreement there.\n3. Get a token: sign in with the Direct account and open `https://oauth.yandex.ru/authorize?response_type=token&client_id=<ClientID>`; copy the `access_token` (it starts with `y0_`) into `YANDEX_DIRECT_TOKEN`. It is valid for about a year and is extended while it is used. It is sent as `Authorization: Bearer ...` and only to api.direct.yandex.com.\n4. Agencies only: set `YANDEX_DIRECT_CLIENT_LOGIN` to the advertiser's login to read that advertiser (sent as `Client-Login`); `yandex_direct_list_agency_clients` lists the logins. Leave it empty for your own account.\n\n**Where to start**: `yandex_direct_get_client` (account, currency), `yandex_direct_list_campaigns`, then `yandex_direct_list_ad_groups`, `yandex_direct_list_ads` and `yandex_direct_list_keywords` with up to 10 `campaign_ids`. Performance numbers come from `yandex_direct_get_report`.\n\n**Money**: object amounts (bids, budgets, Funds) are integers in **micros**: 2500000 = 2.50 in the account currency (`yandex_direct_get_client` gives it). Reports return decimals instead.\n\n**Reports** (`yandex_direct_get_report`): the answer is **tab-separated text**, the first line the column names. `report_name` must be unique for each set of parameters. Small reports come back at once; larger ones are built offline: the answer is then empty with a `retryin` header (seconds). Call again with exactly the same parameters and name after that time. At most 5 offline reports can be queued; search query reports are offline only and cover the last 180 days. With `CUSTOM_DATE` pass `date_from` and `date_to`; with any other period leave them out.\n\n**Paging**: lists return up to `limit` objects (default 500, at most 10,000). If the answer has `LimitedBy`, pass that number as `offset` for the next page.\n\n**Points (units)**: every call spends API points from the advertiser's daily allowance (the `Units` limit); a failed call costs 20. Prefer one call with several ids over many single calls and ask only for the fields you need.\n\n**Errors** arrive as `{\"error\": {\"error_code\", \"error_string\", \"error_detail\"}}` and are passed on as errors: 53 the token is invalid or expired (get a new one, step 3), 54 or 3000/3001 no API access or no rights (the access request of step 2, or a Client-Login the token may not read), 513 the login is not connected to Direct, 152 not enough points today, 506 too many parallel requests, 8000 and 4000 to 4006 a wrong parameter, 8800 not found, 9300 too many ids in one call.\n\n**Out of scope**: creating or editing campaigns, ads, keywords and bids, moderation, budgets and payments, the Sandbox and Wordstat.",
  "region": "intl",
  "category": "advertising",
  "icon": "yandex-direct",
  "docsUrl": "https://yandex.com/dev/direct/doc/en/",
  "prerequisites": "A Yandex Direct account with approved API access (Tools, API in Direct) for an app registered at oauth.yandex.ru with the direct:api permission, and an OAuth token of that account. About 10 minutes plus Yandex's approval time.",
  "requiredEnvVars": [
    "YANDEX_DIRECT_TOKEN"
  ],
  "optionalEnvVars": [
    "YANDEX_DIRECT_CLIENT_LOGIN"
  ],
  "envVarMeta": {
    "YANDEX_DIRECT_TOKEN": {
      "label": "OAuth token",
      "kind": "credential",
      "secret": true,
      "help": "Open https://oauth.yandex.ru/authorize?response_type=token&client_id=<your ClientID> signed in with the Direct account and copy access_token (starts with y0_). The app needs approved Direct API access.",
      "link": "https://oauth.yandex.ru/",
      "pattern": "^(?![Bb]earer|OAuth )[A-Za-z0-9_-]{30,}$",
      "patternMessage": "Paste only the token (it usually starts with y0_), without Bearer or OAuth."
    },
    "YANDEX_DIRECT_CLIENT_LOGIN": {
      "label": "Client login (agencies only)",
      "kind": "setting",
      "help": "Only for agency accounts: the Yandex login of the advertiser to read. Leave empty for your own account.",
      "example": "client-login",
      "pattern": "^[A-Za-z0-9._-]{1,64}$",
      "patternMessage": "The advertiser's Yandex login, letters, digits, dots, dashes."
    }
  },
  "verifyHints": {
    "401": "Yandex Direct refused the token (error 53): it is wrong, expired or revoked. Get a new one at oauth.yandex.ru with your app's ClientID.",
    "403": "The token works, but this account has no Direct API access yet, or the app's access request is not approved (Tools, API in Direct). For agencies, check YANDEX_DIRECT_CLIENT_LOGIN.",
    "429": "Yandex Direct points (units) for today are used up, or too many requests run at once. Wait and verify again."
  },
  "probe": {
    "tool": "yandex_direct_get_client"
  },
  "connector": {
    "name": "Yandex Direct API",
    "type": "REST",
    "baseUrl": "https://api.direct.yandex.com/json/v501",
    "authType": "BEARER_TOKEN",
    "authConfig": {
      "token": "{{YANDEX_DIRECT_TOKEN}}"
    },
    "headers": {
      "Accept": "application/json",
      "Accept-Language": "en",
      "Content-Type": "application/json; charset=utf-8",
      "User-Agent": "AnythingMCP"
    },
    "config": {
      "errorWhen": [
        {
          "path": "error.error_code",
          "in": [
            53
          ],
          "messagePath": [
            "error.error_string",
            "error.error_detail"
          ],
          "status": 401
        },
        {
          "path": "error.error_code",
          "in": [
            54,
            513,
            3000,
            3001,
            58
          ],
          "messagePath": [
            "error.error_string",
            "error.error_detail"
          ],
          "status": 403
        },
        {
          "path": "error.error_code",
          "in": [
            8800
          ],
          "messagePath": [
            "error.error_string",
            "error.error_detail"
          ],
          "status": 404
        },
        {
          "path": "error.error_code",
          "in": [
            152,
            506,
            56
          ],
          "messagePath": [
            "error.error_string",
            "error.error_detail"
          ],
          "status": 429
        },
        {
          "path": "error.error_code",
          "in": [
            52,
            1000,
            1001,
            1002
          ],
          "messagePath": [
            "error.error_string",
            "error.error_detail"
          ],
          "status": 502
        },
        {
          "path": "error.error_code",
          "matches": "^[0-9]+$",
          "messagePath": [
            "error.error_string",
            "error.error_detail"
          ],
          "status": 400
        }
      ]
    }
  },
  "tools": [
    {
      "name": "yandex_direct_get_client",
      "description": "Read the advertiser account the token acts for (or the Client-Login one): ClientId, Login, ClientInfo (name), Currency, CountryId, Type, VatRate, AccountQuality, Archived, CreatedAt and the account's restrictions. Checks the token. Read-only.",
      "parameters": {
        "type": "object",
        "properties": {
          "field_names": {
            "type": "array",
            "items": {
              "type": "string"
            },
            "description": "Fields to return.",
            "default": [
              "ClientId",
              "Login",
              "ClientInfo",
              "Currency",
              "CountryId",
              "Type",
              "VatRate",
              "AccountQuality",
              "Archived",
              "CreatedAt",
              "Restrictions"
            ]
          }
        }
      },
      "endpointMapping": {
        "method": "POST",
        "path": "/clients",
        "headers": {
          "Client-Login": "${YANDEX_DIRECT_CLIENT_LOGIN}"
        },
        "bodyMapping": {
          "method": "get",
          "params": {
            "FieldNames": "$field_names"
          }
        }
      },
      "annotations": {
        "readOnlyHint": true,
        "destructiveHint": false,
        "idempotentHint": true
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "yandex_direct_list_campaigns",
      "description": "List campaigns: Id, Name, Type (TEXT_CAMPAIGN, UNIFIED_CAMPAIGN, SMART_CAMPAIGN, MOBILE_APP_CAMPAIGN, CPM_BANNER_CAMPAIGN ...), Status, State (ON, OFF, SUSPENDED, ENDED, ARCHIVED), StatusPayment, StartDate, EndDate, Currency, Funds and Statistics (all-time clicks and impressions). Optionally the bidding strategy and settings of text or unified campaigns. Read-only.",
      "parameters": {
        "type": "object",
        "properties": {
          "ids": {
            "type": "array",
            "items": {
              "type": "integer"
            },
            "description": "Only these campaign ids."
          },
          "states": {
            "type": "array",
            "items": {
              "type": "string",
              "enum": [
                "ON",
                "OFF",
                "SUSPENDED",
                "ENDED",
                "CONVERTED",
                "ARCHIVED"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Only campaigns in these states."
          },
          "statuses": {
            "type": "array",
            "items": {
              "type": "string",
              "enum": [
                "ACCEPTED",
                "DRAFT",
                "MODERATION",
                "REJECTED"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Only campaigns with these moderation statuses."
          },
          "types": {
            "type": "array",
            "items": {
              "type": "string"
            },
            "description": "Only these campaign types, e.g. TEXT_CAMPAIGN, UNIFIED_CAMPAIGN."
          },
          "field_names": {
            "type": "array",
            "items": {
              "type": "string"
            },
            "description": "Fields to return.",
            "default": [
              "Id",
              "Name",
              "Type",
              "Status",
              "State",
              "StatusPayment",
              "StartDate",
              "EndDate",
              "Currency",
              "Funds",
              "Statistics"
            ]
          },
          "text_campaign_field_names": {
            "type": "array",
            "items": {
              "type": "string"
            },
            "description": "Optional extra fields of text campaigns: BiddingStrategy, Settings, CounterIds, PriorityGoals, AttributionModel, RelevantKeywords, NegativeKeywordSharedSetIds."
          },
          "unified_campaign_field_names": {
            "type": "array",
            "items": {
              "type": "string"
            },
            "description": "Optional extra fields of unified performance campaigns: BiddingStrategy, Settings, CounterIds, PriorityGoals, AttributionModel, TrackingParams, NegativeKeywordSharedSetIds."
          },
          "limit": {
            "type": "integer",
            "minimum": 1,
            "maximum": 10000,
            "default": 500,
            "description": "Objects per page, at most 10000. Default 500. When the answer has LimitedBy, there are more: pass it as offset."
          },
          "offset": {
            "type": "integer",
            "minimum": 0,
            "description": "Skip this many objects (the LimitedBy value of the previous page)."
          }
        }
      },
      "endpointMapping": {
        "method": "POST",
        "path": "/campaigns",
        "headers": {
          "Client-Login": "${YANDEX_DIRECT_CLIENT_LOGIN}"
        },
        "bodyMapping": {
          "method": "get",
          "params": {
            "SelectionCriteria": {
              "Ids": "$ids",
              "States": "$states",
              "Statuses": "$statuses",
              "Types": "$types"
            },
            "FieldNames": "$field_names",
            "TextCampaignFieldNames": "$text_campaign_field_names",
            "UnifiedCampaignFieldNames": "$unified_campaign_field_names",
            "Page": {
              "Limit": "$limit",
              "Offset": "$offset"
            }
          }
        }
      },
      "annotations": {
        "readOnlyHint": true,
        "destructiveHint": false,
        "idempotentHint": true
      }
    },
